def ts(sec):return f'{sec//3600:02}:{sec//60%60:02}:{sec%60:02}'
text=['# Episode 06 — Dad Said HOT… But Meant WARM! | Restaurant English | Funny Family Dinner','','> **Format:** 80 continuous story shots × 15 seconds = **20:00 story runtime**','>','> **Status:** written and illustrated preproduction draft. Creator approval, individual motion first frames, performed voices and video remain pending.','>','> **Story-only:** natural General American family comedy. Optional creator-authored practice belongs after the story; no audience drills, quizzes, narrator recap or timed repetition.','','After their park outing, the Brooks family has a relaxed restaurant dinner. Dan arrives with a grand speech and an imprecise request: hot soup. A server asks whether he means temperature or spice. The family clarifies six individual choices before anything is cooked, enjoys the meal, saves one remaining portion and pays a carefully checked bill. The humor comes from a speech that is never needed and a small question that is.','','## Story arc','','- **00:00–02:00:** plan dinner and an all-in $80 limit; Dan rehearses too much.','- **02:00–04:00:** arrive together, keep six fixed places, ask simply for water.','- **04:00–09:00:** choose six mains; distinguish warm temperature from spicy flavor before submitting one ticket.','- **09:00–12:00:** give cooking real time, receive the correct dishes and check comfortable temperatures.','- **12:00–16:00:** enjoy dinner, pack only Max\'s existing remainder, ask for the check.','- **16:00–20:00:** verify $63.80, pay $80, receive $16.20, leave $10 tip, retain $6.20 and depart together.','','## Performance and continuity rules','',''+ ' '.join(locks), '','Use the unchanged W01 cast and original face/age/body references. Dan\'s watch is on anatomical LEFT wrist; phone/wallet/rehearsal note remain in his RIGHT pocket. Maya and Nina share decisions and authority. SERVER is explicitly off-screen/hands-only and never appears as a new face. Actual editable overlay text governs prices, not generated lettering.','', 'Mild describes flavor, while warm/hot describe temperature; one does not prove the other. Adults check comfortable temperatures before children eat. There is no burning-mouth gag, forced spicy taste, mistaken cooked order, wasteful return or new allergy plot. Washing/cooking/serving/eating/travel need explicit story-time ellipses. No food duplicates or refills across cuts. See [CONTINUITY.md](CONTINUITY.md).','','## Timed story shots','']
for i,(title,cast,loc,camera,action,start,end,dl) in enumerate(rows,1):
    talks=[x.split(':',1) for x in dl.split('/')]
    assert 1<=len(talks)<=3,(i,talks)
    assert sum(len(x[1].split()) for x in talks)<=36,(i,sum(len(x[1].split()) for x in talks))
    b=(i-1)//4+1;p=(i-1)%4+1
    cont='W01 identities and fixed six restaurant places; no unlisted dish, extra diner or new server face. '
    if i<=8:cont='Original kitchen geography and six-person W01 cast. No restaurant food or utensils appear at home. '
    elif i<=16:cont+='No food ordered before the choices and clarification. '
    elif i<=36:cont+='One draft becomes one ticket; soup is corrected before cooking. '
    elif i<=44:cont+='Cooking takes elapsed story time; table stays empty of meals until service. '
    elif i<=59:cont+='Six distinct main dishes decrease only as eaten; mild is not proof of safe temperature. '
    elif i<=64:cont+='Exactly one saved portion transfers once into one box; prompt refrigeration at home. '
    elif i<=72:cont+='Food $58 + tax $5.80 = $63.80; $10 voluntary tip is separate. '
    else:cont+='No extra transaction: $80 - $63.80 = $16.20 change; less $10 tip leaves $6.20. '
    if i in server_shots:cont+='SERVER is an off-screen voice; only anonymous sleeve-covered hands/forearms may enter. '
    text.extend([f'### SHOT_{i:03} | {ts((i-1)*15)}–{ts(i*15)} | {title}','','**Visible cast:** '+', '.join(cast.split(',')),''])
    if i in server_shots:text.extend(['**Off-screen cast:** SERVER',''])
    text.extend([f'**Location:** {loc}','',f'**Camera:** {camera}.','',f'**Action:** {action}','',f'**Opening state:** {start}','',f'**End state:** {end}','',f'**Picture:** [BOARD_{b:02}.png](assets/storyboards/BOARD_{b:02}.png), panel {p}. Illustrated draft; creator approval and individual motion first frame pending.','',f'**Continuity:** {cont.strip()}','','**Dialogue:**',''])
    for who,line in talks:text.extend([f'**{who}:** {line}',''])
(E/'STORY.md').write_text('\n'.join(text))
